apsis (0.6.0-1) noble; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release, see CHANGELOG.md: Restore now works on an
    encrypted Pop!_OS install (LUKS with LVM, the layout the installer's
    "Encrypt drive" makes), on the installation the snapshot was made of;
    other encrypted or LVM layouts stay refused. Once the boot files are
    refreshed, the helper checks that they can still unlock the disk and
    puts the old ones back if they can't. The recovery note starts with the
    lines that unlock the disk. Restore stays experimental; this was run on
    one laptop with that one layout.

 -- atraxsrc <92285717+atraxsrc@users.noreply.github.com>  Tue, 06 Oct 2026 18:55:57 +1100

apsis (0.5.0-1) noble; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release, see CHANGELOG.md: restoring the whole system to a
    snapshot, at the next start (experimental; Pop!_OS 24.04 with
    systemd-boot only), with a safety snapshot first (on by default) and a
    recovery note on the backup disk. The helper's D-Bus interface is now
    Helper3, with a sixth polkit action for the restore. Upgrading,
    reinstalling or removing the package is refused while a job runs (not
    when upgrading from 0.4.x, whose old script doesn't wait), and cancels a
    restore that waits for its restart. A delete cut off part-way leaves a
    dimmed row that Delete removes.

 -- atraxsrc <92285717+atraxsrc@users.noreply.github.com>  Sun, 04 Oct 2026 18:04:31 +1100

apsis (0.4.2-1) noble; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release, see CHANGELOG.md: deleting several snapshots is one
    helper job (DeleteMany), so it works with more than one display; lists
    share a read-only mount and are no longer jobs; a snapshot or delete waits
    for lists instead of being refused; one helper connection per process; the
    applet's desktop entry drops %F.

 -- atraxsrc <92285717+atraxsrc@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 01 Oct 2026 19:30:00 +1000

apsis (0.4.0-1) noble; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release, see CHANGELOG.md: a window laid out like
    Timeshift's in standard COSMIC widgets, settings as tabs (/root and /home
    choices, filter list), stop a running snapshot, jobs shown in every window
    and the panel, leftovers of interrupted snapshots removed, a real "backup
    disk removed" error. Removed: file restore, keep last N, per-user home
    modes. The helper's D-Bus interface is now Helper2; the config file is
    version 2 (converted on the first save; the old one is kept as .bak).

 -- atraxsrc <92285717+atraxsrc@users.noreply.github.com>  Wed, 30 Sep 2026 22:00:00 +1000

